NEARS-3656 QA finding — "Forgot Password?" / "Create Account" links on Sign-In are visually
present, accessibility-exposed with plausible bounds, but a real touch at the exact reported
center produces NO effect: zero navigation, zero Flutter-tag log activity at all (touch does not
even reach the Flutter engine's gesture arena for that frame).

Reproduced on emulator-5556 (unsuffixed control boot, Firebase configured, pid 27932), fresh
Sign-In screen reached via Profile > Login, 6+ independent repro attempts:
- uiautomator-reported bounds: "Forgot Password?" [60,1425][563,1456], "Create Account"
  [837,1425][1284,1456] (see bug-forgot-createaccount-dead-tap-zone.xml, positive control: the
  SAME dump's "Sign In" node [60,1233][1284,1389] tapped normally and triggered field validation
  in the same session, proving the touch/adb pipeline itself is live).
- `adb shell input tap <center>` at (311,1440) and (1060,1440): logcat -d --pid=27932 shows ZERO
  new "flutter" tag lines after the tap (see bug-forgot-createaccount-dead-tap-zone.png), vs.
  "Sign In"/"Continue as Guest"/"Show password" taps in the identical screen which all produced
  immediate, correct effects.
- Retried at 6 different y-offsets within/around the reported band (1400-1470) and via
  `input swipe <same-point> 150ms` — no effect at any of them.
- POSITIVE CONTROL that isolates "hit-test geometry" from "broken callback": keyboard-focus
  traversal (`adb shell input keyevent TAB` x6 + ENTER) DID successfully activate "Create
  Account" and navigated to Sign-Up (and TAB x5 + ENTER activated "Forgot Password?" and
  navigated to Forgot-Password) -- so the onPressed callbacks themselves are wired correctly;
  this is purely a raw-pointer hit-test / semantics-bounds mismatch for this one OverflowBar row.

Root-cause note (not independently proven, flagged for the engineer): the OWNING widget for
these two buttons, UserApp/lib/features/auth/widgets/sign_in/manual_login_widget.dart, is
UNCHANGED by this ticket's diff (git diff 55d5867b8..713788275 -- that file returns empty). The
WRAPPING screen, sign_in_screen.dart, DID change the outer Padding in the same commit range --
fix-cycle 2 (d2fdbf6a5, "UX1 44dp legal-link tap target via advisor-dls Option B") explicitly
removed the Column's bottom padding and trimmed top padding to reclaim vertical space for the
legal links' enlarged ConstrainedBox(tapMin) below this row. That is the same ticket, the same
screen, the same vertical region -- plausible enough to flag as this ticket's own regression
rather than pre-existing, but not confirmed by reverting the padding change and re-testing (out
of QA's write scope / time budget this pass).

Impact: any SIGHTED, TOUCH-only user cannot reach Sign-Up or Forgot-Password from Sign-In's
inline links at default text scale (1.0x) -- only a TalkBack/keyboard-focus user can. Continue as
Guest, Sign In, and the Profile > Login entry point to Sign-In itself are all unaffected.
